@host = http://localhost:3000
@ownerToken = paste-owner-teacher-token
@otherToken = paste-other-teacher-token
@adminToken = paste-admin-token
@courseId = 4

### Registro (repetir para las tres cuentas)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner.teacher@example.test",
  "password": "CourseHub-2026!"
}

### Login del docente propietario
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner.teacher@example.test",
  "password": "CourseHub-2026!"
}

### Crear curso (usar ownerToken)
POST {{host}}/courses
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Arquitectura mantenible",
  "level": "advanced"
}

### 1. Solicitud correcta (docente propietario)
PATCH {{host}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-request-id: demo-correcto

{
  "title": "Arquitectura mantenible (actualizado)"
}

### 2. Identificador inválido
PATCH {{host}}/courses/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-request-id: demo-id-invalido

{
  "title": "No se aplica"
}

### 3. Recurso inexistente
PATCH {{host}}/courses/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-request-id: demo-no-existe

{
  "title": "No se aplica"
}

### 4. Prohibida (docente ajeno)
PATCH {{host}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-request-id: demo-prohibido

{
  "title": "No se aplica"
}

### Extra: administrador sobre el mismo curso
PATCH {{host}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Actualización del administrador"
}
